{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Geun2JtFH6NxP164SCV6ty","type":"tool_result","content":"---\nname: subscription-only-execution-model\ndescription: Curriculum factory prompts run IN Claude Code itself; QA/gates run via the Codex plugin — never a subprocess call to an external LLM CLI/API like gemini.\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: feedback\n  originSessionId: 02e35686-8106-4ecf-b2c9-a4e79962fa68\n  modified: 2026-08-09T20:17:03.292Z\n---\n\nIn `curriculum_builder`, \"live\" execution of the curriculum factory means:\n\n- **Worker/content-generation prompts** (the P0–P6 phase prompts, lesson/unit authoring,\n  anything currently framed as \"the runtime shells out to a model\") are executed **by\n  Claude directly** — i.e. Claude Code itself, acting as the agent, reading the prompt and\n  doing the work in-session under the user's Claude subscription.\n- **QA gates / review / judge steps** are executed **by Codex**, invoked through the\n  already-installed `codex` plugin (e.g. `codex:rescue`, the `claude-codex` plugin tools),\n  under the user's ChatGPT Pro subscription (`~/.codex/auth.json`: `auth_mode: \"chatgpt\"`,\n  `OPENAI_API_KEY: null`).\n\n**Why:** the user has only LLM subscriptions (Claude Code, ChatGPT Pro via Codex) — no\nbilled API keys exist anywhere. Confirmed empty: `GEMINI_API_KEY`, `GOOGLE_API_KEY`,\n`ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, `OPENAI_API_KEY` in shell env and rc files. The `gemini` CLI is\nconfigured for `\"selectedType\": \"gemini-api-key\"` with no key present and is not the\nintended execution path. [[plans/19_curriculum_factory_production_loop_closure]]'s runtime\n(`runtime/capability_cycle.py`, `runtime/routing.py`, `policy/routing/routing_policy.v1.yaml`)\nwas designed around live model routing via subprocess calls to the `gemini` binary as a\ndistinct \"live capability\" probe and cross-family judge — that is the wrong architecture\nfor this user's actual setup, and repeatedly proposing to fix/route through Gemini caused\nmajor, repeated frustration (told directly, explicitly, more than once).\n\n**How to apply:** Any plan or runtime work touching \"live model execution\" in this repo —\nincluding plan 19's routing/capability code and the planned plan 20 (subscription-only\nmodel access) — must route content generation through Claude Code itself and QA/gate\nchecks through the Codex plugin. Never design around, suggest fixing, or fall back to\ndirect API billing or a standalone `gemini` CLI/API call as the execution mechanism, even\nas a stopgap.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e4c8849a-0e6d-4904-b87d-664b63b4cc5f","uuid":"87466138-c5d2-4d1d-88d4-b8201e735e5c","timestamp":"2026-08-12T18:34:03.567Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"---\nname: subscription-only-execution-model\ndescription: Curriculum factory prompts run IN Claude Code itself; QA/gates run via the Codex plugin — never a subprocess call to an external LLM CLI/API like gemini.\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: feedback\n  originSessionId: 02e35686-8106-4ecf-b2c9-a4e79962fa68\n  modified: 2026-08-09T20:17:03.292Z\n---\n\nIn `curriculum_builder`, \"live\" execution of the curriculum factory means:\n\n- **Worker/content-generation prompts** (the P0–P6 phase prompts, lesson/unit authoring,\n  anything currently framed as \"the runtime shells out to a model\") are executed **by\n  Claude directly** — i.e. Claude Code itself, acting as the agent, reading the prompt and\n  doing the work in-session under the user's Claude subscription.\n- **QA gates / review / judge steps** are executed **by Codex**, invoked through the\n  already-installed `codex` plugin (e.g. `codex:rescue`, the `claude-codex` plugin tools),\n  under the user's ChatGPT Pro subscription (`~/.codex/auth.json`: `auth_mode: \"chatgpt\"`,\n  `OPENAI_API_KEY: null`).\n\n**Why:** the user has only LLM subscriptions (Claude Code, ChatGPT Pro via Codex) — no\nbilled API keys exist anywhere. Confirmed empty: `GEMINI_API_KEY`, `GOOGLE_API_KEY`,\n`ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, `OPENAI_API_KEY` in shell env and rc files. The `gemini` CLI is\nconfigured for `\"selectedType\": \"gemini-api-key\"` with no key present and is not the\nintended execution path. [[plans/19_curriculum_factory_production_loop_closure]]'s runtime\n(`runtime/capability_cycle.py`, `runtime/routing.py`, `policy/routing/routing_policy.v1.yaml`)\nwas designed around live model routing via subprocess calls to the `gemini` binary as a\ndistinct \"live capability\" probe and cross-family judge — that is the wrong architecture\nfor this user's actual setup, and repeatedly proposing to fix/route through Gemini caused\nmajor, repeated frustration (told directly, explicitly, more than once).\n\n**How to apply:** Any plan or runtime work touching \"live model execution\" in this repo —\nincluding plan 19's routing/capability code and the planned plan 20 (subscription-only\nmodel access) — must route content generation through Claude Code itself and QA/gate\nchecks through the Codex plugin. Never design around, suggest fixing, or fall back to\ndirect API billing or a standalone `gemini` CLI/API call as the execution mechanism, even\nas a stopgap.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
