{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UxhCH9nphckTh8iuoorh8p","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# N00 result-record schema (frozen)\n2\t\n3\tEvery node result at `plans/26_langgraph_curriculum_factory/results/{node_id}.result.v1.md`\n4\tMUST contain these sections, in order, so the scheduler can recompute status\n5\tfrom evidence rather than trust file presence (per `run.prompt.md` TEST #1).\n6\tA missing required section makes the record inadmissible; the scheduler\n7\ttreats the node as not-yet-`PASSED`.\n8\t\n9\t```markdown\n10\t# {NODE_ID} result\n11\t\n12\tstatus: PASSED | NOT_AVAILABLE | BLOCKED\n13\tgraph_digest: <sha256 of implementation.graph.v2.yaml at execution time>\n14\tnode_prompt: <path> (<sha256 of prompt file>)\n15\tgeneration: <scheduler generation integer this node executed in>\n16\t\n17\t## Inputs\n18\t- predecessor result records consumed, each as `{node_id}: {sha256 of that\n19\t  result record file}`\n20\t- other frozen inputs read (contracts, spec sections, prior artifacts), each\n21\t  with a path and sha256\n22\t\n23\t## Outputs\n24\t- every path in this node's `writes` set from implementation.graph.v2.yaml,\n25\t  each with a sha256 (or `NOT_CREATED` with justification, only permitted\n26\t  where `allowed_results` includes `NOT_AVAILABLE`)\n27\t\n28\t## Commands\n29\t- literal command string, exit code, and evidence path to captured\n30\t  stdout/stderr, for every command run in service of this node (test runs,\n31\t  hash computation, lint, etc.)\n32\t\n33\t## Tests\n34\t- every test name/command required by this node's TEST section, PASS/FAIL,\n35\t  and the exact assertion or count backing that verdict\n36\t\n37\t## Findings\n38\t- open findings this node leaves behind, each with owner (per\n39\t  `rework_edges`), evidence key, and fingerprint; empty list if none\n40\t\n41\t## Invalidated descendants\n42\t- node IDs invalidated by this execution (rework only); empty list on a\n43\t  first-pass PASSED\n44\t\n45\t## Hashes\n46\t- consolidated hash table: every hash referenced above, deduplicated, so a\n47\t  later node can verify without re-deriving\n48\t```\n49\t\n50\t## Status semantics\n51\t\n52\t- `PASSED`: every TEST item verified, every declared `writes` path exists\n53\t  with a recorded hash (unless explicitly `NOT_CREATED` under an\n54\t  `allowed_results` node), no open blocking finding.\n55\t- `NOT_AVAILABLE`: permitted only where the graph's `allowed_results` for\n56\t  that node includes it (currently only `N60_LIVE_PRODUCT_PROOF`); requires a\n57\t  named missing external prerequisite, not an implementation gap.\n58\t- `BLOCKED`: node exhausted its LOOP bound (two repeated same-cause\n59\t  failures) or ownership/spec ambiguity stopped it; findings section MUST\n60\t  name the exact blocking cause.\n61\t\n62\t## Hash discipline\n63\t\n64\tAll hashes use [[digest_algorithm.v1]]. A result record's own file is not\n65\tself-hashed inside itself (unresolvable); the scheduler hashes the result\n66\trecord file externally when a later node cites it as an input.\n67\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e4c8849a-0e6d-4904-b87d-664b63b4cc5f","uuid":"5381dd43-4664-43f5-b1d3-84f770d1fd34","timestamp":"2026-08-12T18:35:42.980Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/filipepinto/Projects/curriculum_builder/plans/26_langgraph_curriculum_factory/contracts/result_record_schema.v1.md","content":"# N00 result-record schema (frozen)\n\nEvery node result at `plans/26_langgraph_curriculum_factory/results/{node_id}.result.v1.md`\nMUST contain these sections, in order, so the scheduler can recompute status\nfrom evidence rather than trust file presence (per `run.prompt.md` TEST #1).\nA missing required section makes the record inadmissible; the scheduler\ntreats the node as not-yet-`PASSED`.\n\n```markdown\n# {NODE_ID} result\n\nstatus: PASSED | NOT_AVAILABLE | BLOCKED\ngraph_digest: <sha256 of implementation.graph.v2.yaml at execution time>\nnode_prompt: <path> (<sha256 of prompt file>)\ngeneration: <scheduler generation integer this node executed in>\n\n## Inputs\n- predecessor result records consumed, each as `{node_id}: {sha256 of that\n  result record file}`\n- other frozen inputs read (contracts, spec sections, prior artifacts), each\n  with a path and sha256\n\n## Outputs\n- every path in this node's `writes` set from implementation.graph.v2.yaml,\n  each with a sha256 (or `NOT_CREATED` with justification, only permitted\n  where `allowed_results` includes `NOT_AVAILABLE`)\n\n## Commands\n- literal command string, exit code, and evidence path to captured\n  stdout/stderr, for every command run in service of this node (test runs,\n  hash computation, lint, etc.)\n\n## Tests\n- every test name/command required by this node's TEST section, PASS/FAIL,\n  and the exact assertion or count backing that verdict\n\n## Findings\n- open findings this node leaves behind, each with owner (per\n  `rework_edges`), evidence key, and fingerprint; empty list if none\n\n## Invalidated descendants\n- node IDs invalidated by this execution (rework only); empty list on a\n  first-pass PASSED\n\n## Hashes\n- consolidated hash table: every hash referenced above, deduplicated, so a\n  later node can verify without re-deriving\n```\n\n## Status semantics\n\n- `PASSED`: every TEST item verified, every declared `writes` path exists\n  with a recorded hash (unless explicitly `NOT_CREATED` under an\n  `allowed_results` node), no open blocking finding.\n- `NOT_AVAILABLE`: permitted only where the graph's `allowed_results` for\n  that node includes it (currently only `N60_LIVE_PRODUCT_PROOF`); requires a\n  named missing external prerequisite, not an implementation gap.\n- `BLOCKED`: node exhausted its LOOP bound (two repeated same-cause\n  failures) or ownership/spec ambiguity stopped it; findings section MUST\n  name the exact blocking cause.\n\n## Hash discipline\n\nAll hashes use [[digest_algorithm.v1]]. A result record's own file is not\nself-hashed inside itself (unresolvable); the scheduler hashes the result\nrecord file externally when a later node cites it as an input.\n","numLines":67,"startLine":1,"totalLines":67}}}
